{"task_id": "Mbpp/90", "solution": "def len_log(words):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the length of the longest word in a list of words.\n    Returns 0 if the list is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not words:\n        return 0\n\n    max_length = 0\n    for word in words:\n        max_length = max(max_length, len(word))\n    return max_length"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "def is_undulating(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a number is undulating, meaning its digits alternate between two distinct values.\n    Single-digit numbers or numbers with identical adjacent digits are not undulating.\n    \"\"\"\n    s = str(abs(n))\n    digits = [int(char) for char in s]\n\n    if len(digits) < 2:\n        return False\n\n    first_digit = digits[0]\n    second_digit = digits[1]\n\n    if first_digit == second_digit:\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(2, len(digits)):\n        if i % 2 == 0:  # Even index, should match first_digit\n            if digits[i] != first_digit:\n                return False\n        else:  # Odd index, should match second_digit\n            if digits[i] != second_digit:\n                return False\n    return True"}
