{"task_id": "Mbpp/100", "solution": "def next_smallest_palindrome(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the next smallest palindrome strictly greater than the given integer.\n    The algorithm handles special cases like all-9s numbers and propagates carries when incrementing the middle section.\n    \"\"\"\n    s = str(n)\n    length = len(s)\n\n    # Special case: if n consists of all '9's (e.g., 9, 99, 999),\n    # the next palindrome will have one more digit, starting and ending with '1'.\n    if all(ch == '9' for ch in s):\n        return int('1' + '0' * (length - 1) + '1')\n\n    # Determine the left half and the middle character (if length is odd)\n    half = length // 2\n    left_part = s[:half]\n    middle_char = s[half] if length % 2 == 1 else ''\n\n    # Construct an initial palindrome candidate by mirroring the left part\n    constructed_palindrome_str = left_part + middle_char + left_part[::-1]\n\n    # If this candidate palindrome is already strictly greater than n, it's our answer.\n    if int(constructed_palindrome_str) > n:\n        return int(constructed_palindrome_str)\n    else:\n        # If not, we need to increment the 'left half (including middle)' part and re-mirror.\n        # This handles cases where mirroring the left produces a number less than or equal to n,\n        # such as 123 -> 121 (not > 123), so we increment to 131.\n        \n        # Form the number representing the left half and middle (if exists)\n        num_to_increment_str = left_part + middle_char\n        incremented_num = int(num_to_increment_str) + 1\n        incremented_num_str = str(incremented_num)\n\n        # Reconstruct the new left_part and middle_char from the incremented string.\n        # If the original length was odd, the last digit of incremented_num_str becomes the new middle.\n        # Otherwise, incremented_num_str directly forms the new left part.\n        if length % 2 == 1:\n            new_left_part = incremented_num_str[:-1]\n            new_middle_char = incremented_num_str[-1]\n        else:\n            new_left_part = incremented_num_str\n            new_middle_char = ''\n\n        # The final palindrome is built by mirroring the new_left_part around the new_middle_char.\n        final_palindrome_str = new_left_part + new_middle_char + new_left_part[::-1]\n        return int(final_palindrome_str)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "_eulerian_cache = {}\ndef eulerian_num(n: int, m: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the Eulerian number a(n, m) using memoized recursion.\n    Handles base cases and uses a global cache for efficiency.\n    \"\"\"\n    if (n, m) in _eulerian_cache:\n        return _eulerian_cache[(n, m)]\n\n    if n == 0 and m == 0:\n        value = 1\n    elif m < 0 or m >= n:\n        value = 0\n    else:\n        # a(n,m) = (n-m)*a(n-1,m-1) + (m+1)*a(n-1,m)\n        term1 = (n - m) * eulerian_num(n - 1, m - 1)\n        term2 = (m + 1) * eulerian_num(n - 1, m)\n        value = term1 + term2\n\n    _eulerian_cache[(n, m)] = value\n    return value"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/102", "solution": "import re\ndef snake_to_camel(s):\n    \"\"\"Converts a snake_case string to CamelCase (PascalCase).\"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return \"\"\n\n    tokens = [token for token in re.split(r\"_+\", s) if token]\n\n    if not tokens:\n        return \"\"\n\n    camel_tokens = []\n    for token in tokens:\n        camel_tokens.append(token[0].upper() + token[1:].lower())\n            \n    return \"\".join(camel_tokens)"}
