{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef max_sub_array_sum_repeated(arr: List[int], n: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest sum of a contiguous subarray in the modified array formed by repeating the given array k times.\n    This uses an efficient O(N) approach with Kadane's algorithm.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Helper function to implement Kadane's algorithm for a single array.\n    def kadane(current_arr: List[int]) -> int:\n        # Assumes current_arr is non-empty as per design context validation.\n        max_ending_here = current_arr[0]\n        max_so_far = current_arr[0]\n        for x in current_arr[1:]:\n            max_ending_here = max(x, max_ending_here + x)\n            max_so_far = max(max_so_far, max_ending_here)\n        return max_so_far\n\n    if not arr: # Handle empty array case: A sum of 0 might be desired if allowed.\n        return 0 # Per assumption if n is len(arr), arr shouldn't be empty for valid inputs.\n\n    if k == 1:\n        # If the array is repeated only once, simply apply Kadane's algorithm to the original array.\n        return kadane(arr)\n\n    # For k > 1, calculate the maximum subarray sum for the array repeated twice.\n    # This covers cases where the maximum subarray spans across the boundary of the original array.\n    arr_repeated_twice = arr + arr\n    max_sum_two_arrays = kadane(arr_repeated_twice)\n\n    # Calculate the total sum of the original array.\n    total_sum_original_array = sum(arr)\n\n    # If the total sum of the original array is positive, and k is greater than 2,\n    # we can potentially increase the maximum sum by adding (k - 2) times the total sum.\n    # This is because if repeating the whole array yields a positive sum, then each additional\n    # full repetition (beyond the first two covered by `max_sum_two_arrays`) will contribute positively.\n    if total_sum_original_array > 0 and k > 2:\n        return max_sum_two_arrays + (k - 2) * total_sum_original_array\n    else:\n        # If the total sum is not positive, or k is 2 (already covered by two arrays),\n        # repeating further will not yield a larger sum than `max_sum_two_arrays`.\n        return max_sum_two_arrays"}
