{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "def max_sum_increasing_subseq(arr, n, i, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence from the prefix arr[0...i-1]\n    and including the element arr[k], where k >= i.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Handle the base case where the prefix is empty.\n    # The only possible increasing subsequence including arr[k] is arr[k] itself.\n    if i == 0:\n        return arr[k]\n\n    # dp[j] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at index j\n    # within the prefix arr[0...i-1].\n    dp = [val for val in arr[:i]]\n\n    # Compute DP for the prefix arr[0...i-1].\n    for j in range(i):\n        for t in range(j):\n            if arr[t] < arr[j] and dp[t] + arr[j] > dp[j]:\n                dp[j] = dp[t] + arr[j]\n\n    # Initialize the maximum sum to arr[k] alone, in case no prefix element\n    # can precede arr[k] to form an increasing subsequence.\n    best_sum = arr[k]\n\n    # Iterate through the prefix to find the best subsequence ending at arr[j]\n    # that can be extended by arr[k].\n    for j in range(i):\n        if arr[j] < arr[k]:\n            candidate_sum = dp[j] + arr[k]\n            if candidate_sum > best_sum:\n                best_sum = candidate_sum\n\n    return best_sum"}
