{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "def set_left_most_unset_bit(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets the left-most (most significant) unset bit in a non-negative integer.\n    If all bits up to the MSB are set, it sets the bit at MSB + 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    msb_pos = n.bit_length() - 1\n\n    unset_pos = None\n    for pos in range(msb_pos, -1, -1):\n        # Check if the bit at 'pos' is 0\n        if not (n >> pos) & 1:\n            unset_pos = pos\n            break\n\n    if unset_pos is not None:\n        # If an unset bit was found, set it.\n        result = n | (1 << unset_pos)\n    else:\n        # If all bits from MSB down to 0 are set, set the bit at msb_pos + 1.\n        result = n | (1 << (msb_pos + 1))\n\n    return result"}
