{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "def get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the maximum sum for n using f(n) = max( (f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n),\n    with memoization using a closure for efficient recursive calls.\n    \"\"\"\n    memo = {}\n\n    def _compute(current_n: int) -> int:\n        if current_n in memo:\n            return memo[current_n]\n\n        if current_n == 0:\n            return 0\n\n        sum_of_parts = (\n            _compute(current_n // 2) +\n            _compute(current_n // 3) +\n            _compute(current_n // 4) +\n            _compute(current_n // 5)\n        )\n\n        result = max(current_n, sum_of_parts)\n        memo[current_n] = result\n        return result\n\n    return _compute(n)"}
