{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "from typing import List, TypeVar\nT = TypeVar(\"T\")\ndef shell_sort(items: List[T]) -> List[T]:\n    \"\"\"Sorts the given array using the Shell sort algorithm.\n    It returns a new list containing the sorted elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    arr = list(items)  # Work on a copy to avoid modifying the original list.\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    # Compute Knuth's gap sequence.\n    gaps = []\n    h = 1\n    while h < n:\n        gaps.append(h)\n        h = 3 * h + 1\n    # Reverse the gaps to iterate in decreasing order, ensuring a gap of 1 is always included.\n    gaps = list(reversed(gaps)) or [1]\n\n    # Perform gapped insertion sort for each gap in the sequence.\n    for gap in gaps:\n        # Perform an insertion sort for elements separated by 'gap'.\n        for i in range(gap, n):\n            # Store the current element to be inserted.\n            temp = arr[i]\n            j = i\n            # Shift elements that are larger than temp to the right.\n            while j >= gap and arr[j - gap] > temp:\n                arr[j] = arr[j - gap]\n                j -= gap\n            # Place temp in its correct sorted position within the gapped subarray.\n            arr[j] = temp\n    return arr"}
