{"task_id": "Mbpp/479", "solution": "def first_Digit(num):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first digit of a given number, ignoring sign and decimal part for floats.\n    Assumes valid numeric input that will always yield a first digit.\n    \"\"\"\n    s = str(num)\n    # Extract the integer part for floats, as per design context\n    s = s.split('.')[0]\n    # Strip any leading sign ('+' or '-'), as per design context\n    s = s[1:] if s.startswith(('+', '-')) else s\n    return int(s[0])"}
